-- title:
--   Common level-stable chart at the ends of the blow-up
-- statement:
--   Throughout, fix primes $q \ge 5$ and $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$, and an integer $M' \ge 1$ with $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` requires a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, pinned by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to $H = \ker\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be non-zero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the classical $j$-series [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (`hj`), let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for a unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the scheme obtained by glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-chart algebra and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra along the middle chart, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal with $\varpi \in y$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of elements $j_0$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no non-zero $\Omega$-point killed by $q$.
--
--   Call $\tau : K \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[L]} K$ a *level automorphism attached to* $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ when [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) holds: for every weight $k$, every pair $f, g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and $p_g \neq 0$, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the $\iota$-image of the Laurent series of $\tau(x)$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\delta$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} \delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/m \\ m\,\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is the Drinfeld-chart input at every supersingular point: for every point $z$ of $\mathfrak{X}$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` and lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` image $z$ satisfying the same supersingularity condition as `hss` (with $y'$ in place of $y$), there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v - fu\bigr)$, subject to seven clauses (summarised here): $e$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to the constant $\sigma(a)$; every level automorphism attached to some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $C$; those attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$ act trivially on $C/y'$; every such $\tau$ acting trivially on $C/y'$ is transported through $e$ by an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ fixing constants whose linear part is a matrix $M$ over $W$ with $M \equiv c\gamma$ entrywise modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ for some $c$ with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, where $c \equiv 1$ if $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$ and $c \not\equiv 1$ if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; prime ideals of $S$ containing $\sigma\varpi$, not containing both $X_0$ and $X_1$, and containing elements $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$ for integers $a_i, b_i$ with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, contract along $e$ to distinct primes of the stalk; for such a prime with tangent datum $(1,0)$, an element $a \in C$ lies in the contracted prime exactly when every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and a Hasse-type clause for [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), asserting that it lies in $K$ and in $C$, differs from the image of some $a_0 \in A$ by an element of $y'$, and that this difference is carried by $e$ to the class of some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0 \ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_i \mathrm{coeff}\,h\cdot a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a, b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   Next, a point $z$, an element $\varpi_z$ with `hϖz`, `hz`, a point $y'$ over $z$ with `hy'` and the supersingularity clause `hss'`, and `hy'y : y'.asIdeal = y` are fixed, together with one Drinfeld chart witness at $z$: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk with $S_1 = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1 - f_1u_1\bigr)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this witness exactly the seven clauses just listed.
--
--   The remaining data are pinned as follows. An ideal $J \subseteq C$ is required by `hJ` to be the infimum of the ideals obtained by pulling back, along the restriction to $C$ of a level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $C$, the contraction along $e_1 \circ (\text{germ at } z)$ of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. A subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ over $A$ is required by `hB` to be $C[\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}]$, with scalars restricted to $A$. A valuation subring $W \subseteq K$ is given with $B \subseteq W$ (`hBW`), and: `hR1` requires $C \subseteq B$ and that every $f \in K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; `hR2` requires $A \to B$ to be formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/\varpi B$ to have Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) requires that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ precisely when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $f \in W$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$; `hEQ` (five clauses) requires: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose zero set is $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with $A \to k$, and equivariant for every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ that preserves $W$, in the sense that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathrm{hAction}\,(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c) \circ \rho$ for some $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in the kernel [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) of $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)\,c^{q+1}$, with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; that level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; that every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit, in that some $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ carries every $b \in B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$ into $B$ and into $Q$; that $b \in B$ is divisible by $\varpi$ as soon as all its translates under such $\tau$ that lie in $B$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and that a level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$. Finally, a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K$ is pinned by `hends`: a subring $O$ belongs to it exactly when there is $a \in J$, non-zero in $K$, such that, with $B_a = C[\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ xa = i\}]$ as an $A$-subalgebra, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ for which $O = \{g/h : g, h \in B_a,\ h \notin P\}$, no element of $y$ that lies in $O$ is a unit in $O$, and $B \not\subseteq O$; and `hperm` requires that every level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ that preserves $W$ permutes these ends, in the sense that for each $O \in$ `ends` there is $O' \in$ `ends` with $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$.
--
--   The conclusion is the existence of an $A$-subalgebra $B_c \subseteq K$ such that: $B_c$ is of finite type over $A$; for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma$, $\tau$ maps $B_c$ into itself; and for every $O \in$ `ends` both $B_c \subseteq O$ and $O$ is the localisation of $B_c$ at the complement of its unit group, in the precise form that $f \in O$ if and only if there are $g, h \in B_c$ with $h$ invertible in $O$ (whenever $h \in O$, its class is a unit of $O$) and $fh = g$.
--
--   This is the first of the three parts into which the analysis of the ends of the blown-up supersingular chart of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ is split: it produces a single finite-type $A$-algebra, stable under the level automorphisms coming from $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, which is contained in every exceptional end and of which every end is a localisation. It is used by the assembled ends statement that combines this common chart with the uniqueness of the translate and the valuative cover, in the study of the Drinfeld local model at a supersingular point.
